Z||000026||AusFiero||09-12-2001||07:12 AM||||Well god damn. I don't think it wants to die. Under the dashboard the wiring is a fused mess. The fuse box is melted also. They came to tow it away today and I drove it out of the garage, yep it started even with a wiring mess. I am going to have a chat to the assessor tomorrow about it. It is a definate write off by the panel shop  but I still want it back. Will probably be able to buy it back cheap and I have another Fiero I can get cheap also so all is not lost yet. I rang tonight about another t-topped 86. But an SE coupe this time. I will need to redo the interior, but that aint a big deal. I can use my fastback rear end on the other car and I will be almost back to normal,  and have 2 sets of t-tops. Or as another option I can get an 88 Formula very cheap, also with t-tops. <BR>It will rise from the ashes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now who knows where I can buy a low mileage Buick 3.8 litre supercharged engine and how much are they stateside? <BR>Thank god for agreed value insurance. Well they set it. I agreed.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
